      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In our previous post, Tokenomics at Scale: How Jamf Built Real-Time Spend Enforcement for Amazon Bedrock , we explained a custom enforcement loop built on AWS IAM Identity Center , Amazon Athena over Amazon Bedrock model invocation logs , and AWS Lambda .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The approach relies on three things: IAM principal attribution , which Amazon Bedrock records automatically; AWS Cost and Usage Reports (CUR) 2.0 or AWS Cost Explorer for reporting; and AWS Budgets with budget actions for enforcement.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon Bedrock captures the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) principal identity, the IAM user or role , for every inference request.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon Bedrock accessed through IAM roles or IAM users.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A CUR 2.0 data export and an Amazon Simple Storage Service ( Amazon S3 ) bucket to receive it.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You can apply up to 50 principal or session tags per IAM user or role.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Point Amazon Athena at the CUR 2.0 export to group spend by iamPrincipal/team and usage type:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Available actions include applying a custom IAM policy, applying a service control policy (SCP), and targeting Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) or Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) instances.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "CUR does not contain per-request line items : Both classic CUR and CUR 2.0 aggregate Amazon Bedrock cost by usage type, operation, and pricing/resource attributes over an hour or a day.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:29:55.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:45.520Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "IAM principal fields require CUR 2.0 : The legacy CUR format does not include them.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/tokenomics-at-scale-track-and-cap-amazon-bedrock-spend-per-iam-principal-with-cur-2-0-and-aws-budgets/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
